#: Game.Levels.Congruence.L02_mod_symm
msgid "If §0, is it true that §1?\n"
"\n"
"Before we dive into the math, let's learn a crucial syntactic trick: the **§2** keyword.\n"
"By default, tactics like §3 or §4 only apply to your *goal*. But often you need to modify your *hypotheses* (your assumptions).\n"
"* §5 will unfold the definition only inside the hypothesis §6.\n"
"* §7 will unfold it *everywhere* (in all hypotheses and the goal at once).\n"
"* You can also do this with rewrites: §8 will rewrite using §9 inside §10.\n"
"\n"
"Start this proof by typing §11. Then let's unpack the algebra:\n"
"We assume §12, so §13.\n"
"We need to prove §14, which means §15.\n"
"Since §16, the multiplier should be §17.\n"
"\n"
"You will need an intermediate mathematical step. You can create one using the §18 tactic.\n"
"If you type §19, Lean will add §20 to your context.\n"
"You can then use §21 to transform your goal!\n"
"\n"
"**Rewriting backwards**\n"
"By default, §22 looks for the *left* side of your equality (§23) and replaces it with the *right* side (§24).\n"
"If you ever formulate your equality the other way around, for example §25, you will need to tell Lean to rewrite from right to left using a left arrow: §26.\n"
"*(To type the left arrow §27, simply type §28 and press Space)*"
msgstr ""

#. §0: $m$
#: Game
msgid "# Welcome to the Number Theory Game\n"
"#### An introduction to integer arithmetic and formal proofs.\n"
"\n"
"In this game, we will explore the fascinating world of Number Theory.\n"
"We will start from the basic definition of divisibility and build our way up\n"
"to modular arithmetic and congruences.\n"
"\n"
"Our ultimate goal is to understand how remainders work, how to safely manipulate\n"
"equations modulo §0, and eventually reach powerful results like the\n"
"Chinese Remainder Theorem. We will do this by solving levels in a computer\n"
"puzzle game called Lean.\n"
"\n"
"# Read this.\n"
"\n"
"Learning how to use an interactive theorem prover takes time.\n"
"Tests show that the people who get the most out of this game are\n"
"those who read the help texts on the left side of the screen.\n"
"\n"
"To start, click on the **Divisibility Club**."
msgstr ""

