#: Game.Levels.GCD.L04_coprime_forward
msgid "Two integers §0 and §1 are called **coprime** (or *relatively prime*) exactly when their greatest common divisor is §2: §3.\n"
"\n"
"By our definition, this immediately gives us a Bézout identity: there exist integers §4 with §5.\n"
"\n"
"*Note:* an \"if and only if\" statement like this one is always split into two separate levels in this game — one per direction of the arrow. This level is the \"§6\" direction; the next one is \"§7\".\n"
"\n"
"This direction is really just unpacking the definition: §8 to get access to the pieces, §9 to peel them apart, and hand the pieces straight back with §10."
msgstr ""

