#: Game.Levels.Divisibility.L01_first_proof
msgid "**Divisibility (§0)**\n"
"\n"
"We say that an integer §1 **divides** an integer §2 (written as §3) if §4 is a multiple of §5.\n"
"Formally, this means there exists some integer §6 such that:\n"
"§7\n"
"\n"
"**Examples:**\n"
"* §8 is true because §9 (here our witness is §10).\n"
"* §11 is true because §12 (here §13).\n"
"* §14 is true because §15 (here §16).\n"
"* §17 is **false**, because there is no integer §18 that makes §19.\n"
"\n"
"**How it works in Lean:**\n"
"When you see §20 in your goal, Lean translates this under the hood to an \\\\\"exists\\\\\" statement: §21.\n"
"To prove it, you must provide the exact value of §22 using the §23 tactic (for example, §24)."
msgstr ""

