#: Game.Levels.Defs
msgid "**Modular Congruence (§0)**\n"
"\n"
"We say that §1 is **congruent** to §2 modulo §3 if their difference §4 is a multiple of §5.\n"
"Formally, it means §6 divides §7:\n"
"§8\n"
"\n"
"**Intuition:**\n"
"This is a mathematical way of saying that §9 and §10 leave the *same remainder* when divided by §11. Think of a clock: 15:00 and 3:00 point to the same place because §12.\n"
"\n"
"**Examples:**\n"
"* §13 because §14, which simplifies to §15.\n"
"* §16 because §17, which is §18.\n"
"* §19 because §20, which is §21.\n"
"\n"
"**How it works in Lean:**\n"
"We created a custom notation §22 to represent a function called §23. When you see this notation in your goal or hypotheses, you can use the §24 tactic. This will strip away the formatting and reveal the underlying divisibility statement: §25."
msgstr ""

