#: Game.Levels.GCD.L09_gcd_shift
msgid "Welcome to the final boss of World 3!\n"
"\n"
"We prove the fact that sits at the heart of the **Euclidean Algorithm**: shifting a number by a multiple of §0 does not change its greatest common divisor with §1.\n"
"\n"
"Formulation: if §2 is a (non-negative) gcd of §3 and §4, and §5 is a (non-negative) gcd of §6 and §7, then §8.\n"
"\n"
"**Strategy** (this is a long one — take it one step at a time!):\n"
"\n"
"1. Show §9 is also a common divisor of §10 and §11 (not just of §12): since §13, and §14 divides both §15 and §16, it divides §17 too. Now §18 is a common divisor of §19 and §20, and §21 is *the greatest one* (Level 3!), so §22.\n"
"2. Symmetrically, show §23 is also a common divisor of §24 and §25: since §26 divides both §27 and §28, it divides the combination §29 too. Applying Level 3 again (this time with §30 as \"the greatest\"), you get §31.\n"
"3. Finally, §32 and §33, together with §34 and §35, give §36 by the antisymmetry lemma (§37) that has just been added to your inventory!"
msgstr ""

